n\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy","abstract":[{"text":"Whether, and on what terms, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that is a URL is resolved by fetching the document","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it names (T21.5, ","type":"text"},{"code":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). # Why this is one nested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"do we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — and none of them means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anything without [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::allow_http","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}]},{"text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this tenant’s"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domains or ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}]},{"text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument [","type":"text"},{"code":"OidcPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes for ","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". # Every bound here is a security control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::min_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::max_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row written by hand cannot lift them.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is which is the whole of what [","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_tenant_override","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"clamp_overrides_to_org","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"], validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the mirror image of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"mfa_enforced","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], on the ladder ","type":"text"},{"code":"disabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"initial_access_token","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" →","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymous","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a tenant may move down it and never up. * [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_max_clients","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], on the ordinary ","type":"text"},{"code":"tenant <= org","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rule — with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrinkle that ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the second means ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never sweep"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", which is the longest window of all and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is handled by [","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_ttl_strictness","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", therefore never validated against the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"baseline and never clamped: * [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::default_locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. A language is a presentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preference; there is no sense in which Italian is stricter than French. *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. Each names per-tenant resources — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant’s MCP servers, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" tenant’s callback hosts — and there is no sense in which one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would force an organization to enumerate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline before any tenant could name one. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more restrictive”, which binds every field that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"has"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a restrictiveness; a field that has none cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both groups and is checked on the resolved policy rather than on either input: see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_dcr_policy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"OidcPolicy","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"AxiamSDK","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"}}}